{"tool_name":"fba","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"fba","home":"https://github.com/jlduan/fba","license":"MIT","summary":"FBA is a flexible and streamlined Python package to perform quality control, quantification, demultiplexing, multiplet detection, clustering and visualization of feature barcoding assays.","addition_date":"2021-09-08T16:40:40Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:19:24.701627Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:fba","credit":[{"email":"Gary.Hon@utsouthwestern.edu","name":"Gary Hon","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1615-0391","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://fba.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"}]}],"name":"FBA","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab375","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Single cell RNA-Seq (scRNA-Seq) has broadened our understanding of cellular heterogeneity and provided valuable insights into cellular functions. Recent experimental strategies extend scRNA-Seq readouts to include additional features, including cell surface proteins and genomic perturbations. These 'feature barcoding' strategies rely on converting molecular and cellular features to unique sequence barcodes, which are then detected with the transcriptome. Results: Here, we introduce FBA, a flexible and streamlined package to perform quality control, quantification, demultiplexing, multiplet detection, clustering and visualization of feature barcoding assays. Availabilityand implementation: FBA is available on PyPi at htt